    "body": "Adds production-oriented Sign in with Apple on top of the merged provider-neutral authentication foundation.\n\nSecurity and flow:\n- server-generated one-time state + nonce challenges; only SHA-256 hashes are persisted\n- pessimistic locking and single consumption to prevent replay\n- short-lived ES256 Apple client secret generated from the server-only .p8 key\n- authorization code exchanged by the API at Apple's token endpoint\n- the API validates the Apple-issued ID token against Apple's JWK set, issuer, audience, expiry and exact nonce\n- the browser never decides whether an Apple identity is trusted\n- returning users resolve by stable Apple `sub`; Apple email is not used as the durable identity key\n- existing doFast accounts are never silently linked merely because Apple returns the same email\n- new Apple users receive the normal doFast user + wallet + JWT flow\n\nWeb/config:\n- official Sign in with Apple JS button on login and registration\n- Docker and production Compose wiring for public client/redirect values and server-only Team/Key/private-key settings\n- V14 challenge migration and account/auth documentation\n\nTests cover challenge hashing/single-use semantics and Apple account creation/linking boundaries.",
